INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S COTTAGE - KITCHEN - NIGHT

A storm presses at the windows. A single oil lamp. A cracked radio on the sill. Bread dough rises under a damp cloth.

TAMSIN HOLLOWAY, 15, wool sweater, sleeves pushed up, kneads at the table. She is alone. She talks to the dough.

TAMSIN
You'll be fine. You're a good loaf. Don't listen to the wind.

The radio hisses. She wipes her hands on her apron and turns the dial.

RADIO (V.O.)
(crackling)
...coast guard advises all small craft... gale force... off Marrow Point...

She turns it up. Frowns.

TAMSIN
That's us.

She checks the clock. 9:40. Pulls on a coat. Picks up the lamp.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
Dad said stay inside. Dad also said the light never fails.

She opens the back door. Wind slams it wide. She shoves it closed, hard, then tries again, shoulder first.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE STAIRS - CONTINUOUS

Narrow iron steps spiral up into the dark. Tamsin climbs, lamp swinging.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Seventy-two steps. Seventy-two. Don't count the missing one.

Halfway up, the radio in her coat pocket crackles. She stops. Pulls it out.

RADIO (V.O.)
(faint)
Keeper, come in. Keeper Holloway, do you read?

TAMSIN
It's Tamsin. Dad's in town. The boat didn't come back.

RADIO (V.O.)
(pause, static)
Understood. How is your light?

TAMSIN
Dark. I'm going up.

At the top, the lantern room. A hulking brass mechanism, silent. Salt crusts the glass. And at the far side, crouched in the shadow:

An old man in an oilskin coat. ELIAS MARRIOT, 70s, beard like seaweed. His hands tremble over a half-broken gear.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
(freezing)
Who are you?

ELIAS
Don't be frightened. I came to fix it.

TAMSIN
Nobody fixes it but us.

ELIAS
Your father asked me. Years ago. Said if the light ever failed.

TAMSIN
He never told me about you.

ELIAS
He wouldn't.

Elias lifts the gear in both hands. It gleams, wet with oil. Tamsin sets the lamp down on the floor and kneels beside him.

TAMSIN
Show me.

ELIAS
Hold it steady.

She does. He threads a bolt. The mechanism groans. Wind howls at the glass.

RADIO (V.O.)
Keeper, I have a trawler off Marrow Point. They need your beam.

TAMSIN
(shouting at the radio)
Ten minutes!

Elias turns the final bolt. The gear catches. A great shuddering sweep of light cuts out across the black water.

Tamsin laughs, breathless. Elias smiles, slow and tired.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
Seventy-two steps.

ELIAS
Seventy-three. You forgot the one you made.

She looks out at the beam, wide and white, finding the sea.
